## Figure naming convention
- `fig_slideNN_*` tracks **deck position**, not roadmap number — so the files must be renumbered whenever the deck is reordered.
- `fig_appendix_slideNN_*` is backup material for slide NN; `fig_appendix_*` with no number has no home slide.
- Slides 12, 13 and 15 are hand-built graphics with no generating code in the repo — they can only be edited at the source that made them.
- PowerPoint re-encodes images on insert (longest edge capped at 2048), so an embedded image never byte-matches the repo PNG. To check whether the deck is current, compare visually or by image similarity, not by hash.
- Do not re-execute notebooks 03/04 just to refresh outputs — clustering re-runs can perturb the validated silhouette and ARI numbers.

## Data sources
- **Food_Product_Emissions.csv** — Poore & Nemecek (2018), per-kg food LCA, via Our World in Data. *Slides 4, 6, 7, 8, 9.*
- **ghg-emissions.csv** — Climate Watch, global GHG by sector 1990–2023. Units are **MtCO2e (million tonnes)**. *Slides 2, 3.*
- **ReFED_surplus_table(Surplus Data).csv** — ReFED 2024 data, published in 2025 sector fact sheets; US surplus food by sector, tonnage and associated GHG. *Slides 10, 11, 14.* Also read by 05_playbook, but only for its appendix residential-surplus context number.
- **ghg-per-protein-poore.csv** — OWID, emissions per 100 g protein. *Slide 5.* (metadata/readme sidecars alongside in `data/`)
